[TITLE]
NUM-49: junction J1 takes a 1 cfs DWF carrying TN = 10 mg/L and TSS = 10 mg/L.
Treatment at J1: TN's removal is written in terms of itself (a cycle),
and TSS has a concentration-type equation that does not involve TN.
TN is listed before TSS, so TN's removal is evaluated first.
Treatment can only remove mass: TSS at J1 and at the outfall must not exceed
the 10 mg/L it arrives with (its equation asks for 9 mg/L).

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
FLOW_ROUTING         KINWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE    01/01/2020
REPORT_START_TIME    00:00:00
END_DATE             01/01/2020
END_TIME             04:00:00
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
DRY_STEP             01:00:00
ROUTING_STEP         30

[POLLUTANTS]
;;Name  Units  Crain  Cgw  Crdii  Kdecay
TN      MG/L   0      0    0      0
TSS     MG/L   0      0    0      0

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev  MaxDepth  InitDepth  SurDepth  Aponded
J1      110   5         0          0         0

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev  Type
O1      100   FREE

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  From  To  Length  Roughness  InOffset  OutOffset  InitFlow
C1      J1    O1  400     0.013      0         0          0

[XSECTIONS]
;;Link  Shape     Geom1  Geom2  Geom3  Geom4  Barrels
C1      CIRCULAR  2      0      0      0      1

[DWF]
;;Node  Constituent  Baseline
J1      FLOW         1
J1      TN           10
J1      TSS          10

[TREATMENT]
;;Node  Pollutant  Function
J1      TN         R = 0.5*R_TN
J1      TSS        C = 0.9*TSS

[REPORT]
NODES ALL
LINKS ALL
